                <pb facs="1268" n="1262" sameAs="frus:frus1894app2/pg1262"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Willis to Mr. Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 13.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Honolulu, Hawaiian Islands</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1893-12-14"><hi rendition="#italic">December
                                14, 1893</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of Department dispatch, No. 5, inclosing two copies of the report of the
                    electrical congress held in Chicago August 19, 1893, in the matter of units of
                    electrical measure.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Albert S. Willis</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
